        <item>
            <title>0.18.20</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 17:08:19 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.18.20</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.18.20</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.18.20</h2>
<ul>
<li>**Window snaps land in Zen and Firefox, instantly** — Rayto now switches off the app&#x27;s animated accessibility mode while it moves a window, the way Rectangle does, so a half or a corner appears at once at the size you asked for.</li>
<li>**Safeguards and options always in view** — the pill editor no longer hides them behind a &quot;More&quot; row.</li>
<li>**&quot;Move into a new folder&quot; is gone** from the pill editor — wrap a pill into a folder in the menu&#x27;s folder mode instead.</li>
<li>**Links in a new window** — a link pill can open its page in a new browser window instead of a tab: on by default for a new link pill, switch it off in the pill if you want a tab. Works with Safari, Zen, Firefox, Chrome, Arc, Brave, Edge, Vivaldi, Opera.</li>
<li>**No shimmer on pills with an alternative** — their faces no longer tremble while the menu opens.</li>
<li>**Problem reports that help** — Rayto now keeps a diagnostic log on your Mac by default, so a report you send carries what happened. The log never leaves your Mac by itself. Switch it off in Settings, under About.</li>
<li>**One Report a Problem** — the menu bar and Settings open the same panel: your words plus a readable diagnostic file, as an email draft you see before sending.</li>
<li>**A cleaner install window** — the disk image opens in Finder&#x27;s own light or dark window, like other Mac apps, with readable labels.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
